    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0687" n="597" xml:id="pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.825/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-11T17:00:00+08:00">December 11, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 11—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed by Japanese colleague compulsory pilotage not in existence in
                    Japan. Possibly an error made in paragraph 5 of my November 24, 2 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="90" xml:id="d501-f1"/> therefore request that I be informed at earliest
                    possible date whether compulsory pilotage exists by law in principal United
                    States ports for merchant vessels.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d501-f1" n="90" xml:id="d501-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 1006, November 25, 1931, from the Minister in China, <ref
                        target="#pg594">p. 594</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
